# Run bsfmt After Editing BrightScript Files

After making any edits to a `.brs` file, run the formatter:

```
npx bsfmt <path/to/file.brs>
```

This is **mandatory** — the CI "Check formatting consistency" step will fail if skipped.

## Key rules enforced by bsfmt.json

- `Function` / `End Function` (Title case) — not `function` / `end function`
- `AND` / `OR` (uppercase) — not `and` / `or`
- All other keywords lowercase (`if`, `then`, `end if`, `for`, `return`, etc.)
- 2-space indentation (spaces, not tabs)
- Comments use `'` single-quote style
- No trailing whitespace
- Spaces inside non-empty `{}` braces
- Multi-line objects/arrays are formatted consistently

## Example

After editing `HomeScreenHelpers.brs`:

```
npx bsfmt src/channel/components/controllers/ContentController/HomeScreenHelpers.brs
```

If editing multiple files, run bsfmt on each one individually.
